{"nodes": [{"id": "chicken_behavior_analysis_main_chicken_behavior_analysis_main_img_test_frame00801", "label": "Test Frame 00801 - Siren Camera IR View 28 Seconds After Frame 00301", "file_type": "image", "source_file": "Chicken-Behavior-Analysis-main/Chicken-Behavior-Analysis-main/img_test/frame00801.png", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Monochrome 1080P-IPC-Siren frame timestamped 2022-02-22 08:14:44, the same pen and identical camera pose as frame00301 but 28 seconds later. The feed line and five pans are pixel-aligned with frame00301 while the birds have redistributed: the rosettes around the pans are looser and more animals have moved to the upper right corner."}, {"id": "chicken_behavior_analysis_main_chicken_behavior_analysis_main_img_test_frame00801_temporal_frame_pair", "label": "Near-Duplicate Temporal Frame Pair", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "Chicken-Behavior-Analysis-main/Chicken-Behavior-Analysis-main/img_test/frame00801.png", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "frame00301 and frame00801 share a static background and differ only in bird placement, so the pair isolates the moving foreground from the fixed scene. Useful for background subtraction or motion-based validation, but it also means the two frames are not statistically independent test samples - scoring them as such inflates apparent accuracy."}, {"id": "chicken_behavior_analysis_main_chicken_behavior_analysis_main_img_test_frame00801_reduced_feeder_crowding", "label": "Reduced Feeder Crowding Between Frames", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "Chicken-Behavior-Analysis-main/Chicken-Behavior-Analysis-main/img_test/frame00801.png", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Compared with frame00301 the pans are surrounded by visibly fewer birds and the litter around them is exposed, showing measurable turnover at the feeding stations within half a minute. Feeder occupancy is therefore a fast-changing time series, which argues for sampling frames densely if feeding-time statistics are the target output."}, {"id": "chicken_behavior_analysis_main_chicken_behavior_analysis_main_img_test_frame00801_illumination_domain_variation", "label": "Cross-Channel Illumination Domain Variation", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "Chicken-Behavior-Analysis-main/Chicken-Behavior-Analysis-main/img_test/frame00801.png", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The test folder mixes flat monochrome IR frames (Siren) with brightly lit colour frames (PIR, Gas) of visually different pens. This is an intentional domain shift: a model that generalises must handle both, and grayscale/colour-jitter augmentation during training is effectively mandated by the composition of this evaluation set."}], "edges": [{"source": "chicken_behavior_analysis_main_chicken_behavior_analysis_main_img_test_frame00801", "target": "chicken_behavior_analysis_main_chicken_behavior_analysis_main_img_test_frame00301_camera_1080p_ipc_siren", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "Chicken-Behavior-Analysis-main/Chicken-Behavior-Analysis-main/img_test/frame00801.png", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "chicken_behavior_analysis_main_chicken_behavior_analysis_main_img_test_frame00801", "target": "chicken_behavior_analysis_main_chicken_behavior_analysis_main_img_test_frame00301_pan_feeder_line", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "Chicken-Behavior-Analysis-main/Chicken-Behavior-Analysis-main/img_test/frame00801.png", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "chicken_behavior_analysis_main_chicken_behavior_analysis_main_img_test_frame00801",